%I A014543 #21 Aug 29 2026 09:27:00
%S A014543 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,4,9,23,42,70,105,154,226,326
%N A014543 Crossing counts in toroidal drawings of K_n exhibited by Guy, Jenkyns and Schaer (1968).
%C A014543 For 1 <= n <= 10, a(n) = cr_1(K_n), the toroidal crossing number of K_n. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Aug 29 2026
%C A014543 For 11 <= n <= 16, the exhibited drawings establish only cr_1(K_n) <= a(n); Guy, Jenkyns and Schaer conjectured equality for n=11. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Aug 29 2026
%C A014543 The terms form the finite construction table published in the cited paper; they are not values of a closed formula. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Aug 29 2026
%D A014543 Martin Gardner, Crossing Numbers. Ch. 11 in Knotted Doughnuts and Other Mathematical Entertainments. New York: W. H. Freeman, 1986.
%H A014543 Richard K. Guy, Tom Jenkyns and Jonathan Schaer, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0021-9800(68)80063-8">The Toroidal Crossing Number of the Complete Graph</a>, J. Combin. Theory 4 (1968), 376-390.
%H A014543 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CompleteGraph.html">Complete Graph</a>.
%H A014543 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ToroidalCrossingNumber.html">Toroidal Crossing Number</a>.
%e A014543 a(7) = 0 and a(8) = 4.
%K A014543 nonn,nice,fini,changed
%O A014543 1,8
%A A014543 _Eric W. Weisstein_
